## Manual notices

The following notices cover source and native components whose attribution is
not fully represented by Rust crate metadata in `cargo about`.

### Render fixture corpus (`render-fixtures/`)

The render fixture corpus was imported from the `render-repros/` directory of the
reference implementation (Obscura, upstream `h4ckf0r0day/obscura`), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The fixtures, their colour-component behaviour checks
(`color-checks.json`) and the checker they derive from (`render-fixtures/tools/check.py`)
carry that license; see `render-fixtures/ATTRIBUTION.md` for the exact source revision.
The Chromium reference captures (`chromium.png`, `checks.json`) were produced by this
project and are Apache-2.0 like the rest of the repository.

### Vendored forks (`crates/tenta-h2/`)

`tenta-h2` is a fork of [`h2`](https://github.com/hyperium/h2) v0.4.19 by Carl Lerche
and Sean McArthur, licensed under the MIT License. The upstream sources, its
integration test suite and its `LICENSE` file are vendored unchanged except for the
HTTP/2 client fingerprint patch documented in `crates/tenta-h2/TENTA-PATCH.md`; the
crate keeps the MIT license of the original. The upstream HPACK story fixture corpus
is not vendored.

### Native QuickJS forks (`crates/tenta-quickjs-{core,sys}/`)

The renamed `tenta-quickjs-core` and `tenta-quickjs-sys` packages derive from
[rquickjs](https://github.com/DelSkayn/rquickjs) 0.12.2 at revision
`635f9322ccc875e3f9851e7f75ec538cf3274fd5`, under the MIT License. Their
`UPSTREAM.json` files record exact crates.io archive checksums. The binding
license omitted from the upstream core/sys archives is retained from the
same-version facade archive. The sys package bundles QuickJS-ng 0.15.1 with
its original MIT license and copyright notices in `quickjs/LICENSE`.
The native hook and ownership changes are documented in
`crates/tenta-quickjs-core/TENTA-PATCH.md`; `upstream-diff.patch` records the
source delta. These are local unpublished forks, not original upstream releases.

### Local V8 bindings and native patch (`crates/tenta-v8/`)

`tenta-v8` derives its Rust binding files from MIT-licensed rusty_v8 152.2.0
(Deno authors), crate SHA-256
`a10fe1a92da5c32c7c7f838ce36c0ccfcfd5edf0865b58bdde820aa64cea9888`.
The recorded VCS revision is `2768994f664e8a6e3aba27503606c58339136e2a` with the
upstream dirty flag set; the crate checksum identifies the actual source.
Original headers and the restored exact upstream MIT license are retained.
TentaBrowser's local changes are Apache-2.0.

The matched native archive derives from BSD-licensed V8 15.2.124.1 with the
opt-in legacy property hooks and native ordinary-record classifier. Source and
build records pin the native dependencies and toolchains. The companion
[notice index](crates/tenta-v8/native/notices/NOTICES.md) retains 91 exact upstream
notice files covering the observed macOS arm64 components and a disclosed
optional/build-tool superset. The native23 applicability record relates the
unchanged base component inventory to the two-action binding-object/archive
increment; it is not a new complete inventory or other-target review.

Retain that directory, original headers and the binding MIT/local Apache licenses
with redistributed source/native artifacts. Source reconstruction, native tests,
artifact routing, browser behavior and distribution-specific obligations have
separate evidence. No package or native archive is published by this preparation.
